135
00:17:15.319 --> 00:17:17.660
David Millar-Durrant: There's zero row overhead.

136
00:17:17.670 --> 00:17:35.579
David Millar-Durrant: You also get nice things like you have optional super-efficient tagging of data types to stop hash collisions, you can do, sort of, typing of the unserialized data optionally as well. There's lots of nice tricks, there's, ways of checking drift in APIs automatically, and all of this is, again, very standard and used a lot.

137
00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:38.020
